{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511871-auspice-preview-except-ahroun-for-w5","id":1511871,"title":"Auspice-Preview (except Ahroun) for W5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-17T08:48:53-07:00","id":1511871,"title":"Auspice-Preview (except Ahroun) for W5","content":"<div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img data-align=\"center\" data-linkurl=\"https://imgur.com/a/7BUmzoQ\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/c7w5P4U.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/c7w5P4U.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/c7w5P4U.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> <br /> A couple of thoughts:<ul><li>Strange to not do two double-pages this time around in order to show off all the Auspices.</li> <li>I'm a bit disappointed that none of the mechanics have been previewed thus far.</li> <li>The Ragabash: &quot;Not least because \u201cthe way things have always been done\u201d has resulted in Apocalypse.\u200b&quot; Okay, which is why all the young Garou are supposed to be skeptical of Garou-traditions now, I thought...?</li> <li>I have to say I really don't like the Galliard and Philodox-parts... I'm not a fan of that particular writer's style. It's convoluted to the point of finding different ways to say the same thing repeatedly (you could've saved a lot of words by just saying that some Philodox are truthseekers above all when it comes to matters of justice and some are traditionalists). And there's this habit of trying to phrase things in bizarre ways. Like, for example, &quot;others spin gripping yarns of context and sociological understanding\u200b&quot;... &quot;spinning yarns of context&quot;...? But then sometimes the tone suddenly becomes almost conversational (like &quot;Philodoxes in play might expect to evaluate secrets a cagey ally has, uh, \u201cdiscovered,\u201d\u200b &quot;). I didn't like this particular writer's style in the V5 Players Guide (there's this very rambly write-up about the new Project-mechanics that is similar to this) and I don't like it here either.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T09:24:04-07:00","id":1511873,"title":"","content":"What's with the art? Did they take some concept images from V5 or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T10:16:24-07:00","id":1511881,"title":"","content":"Also with the number of humans we've seen thus far in the Tribe-previews and this, I'm wondering why they even bothered with wolf-born Garou still being a thing in W5. Clearly, the focus is on the idea that your character started out as human - and the Lupus-Garou are a complete afterthought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T10:32:43-07:00","id":1511883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511871-auspice-preview-except-ahroun-for-w5?p=1511881#post1511881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also with the number of humans we've seen thus far in the Tribe-previews and this, I'm wondering why they even bothered with wolf-born Garou still being a thing in W5. Clearly, the focus is on the idea that your character started out as human - and the Lupus-Garou are a complete afterthought.</div> </div> </div> </div>The pictures are so simplified, too. The Raggie is a dude in a hoodie, the Theurge could stand in for a baali, the philodox is a goddamn librarian and Galliard is very hard trying to be a Fianna.<br /> <br /> Come on artists, you have 5 forms to play with, use 'em!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T10:55:58-07:00","id":1511886,"title":"","content":"The fact that all four have the exact same structure bugs me. It's like a fill-in the blank section:<br /> <br /> &quot;Changed of the sign of the [blank] moon, they do [blank].<br /> <br /> Than can [blank] in [blank] way, or in [blank] way. Or that do it [blank] way or [blank] way, as long as whatever they're doing is still [blank].<br /> <br /> Expect them to do [blank], [blank], [blank] and [blank].&quot;<br /> <br /> For such short write-ups, it's really unpleasant to read that back to back.<br /> <br /> I'm also really not-grooving on the new Auspice glyphs. The Ragabash and Theurge just have extra marks that don't communicate enough, while the Philodox and Galliards communicate too much by relying on symbolism tied to specific cultures (scales as a sign of justice, a lyre as a the sign of a storyteller).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T11:19:44-07:00","id":1511891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511871-auspice-preview-except-ahroun-for-w5?p=1511886#post1511886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also really not-grooving on the new Auspice glyphs. The Ragabash and Theurge just have extra marks that don't communicate enough, while the Philodox and Galliards communicate too much by relying on symbolism tied to specific cultures (scales as a sign of justice, a lyre as a the sign of a storyteller).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I didn't look too closely at the Auspice-glyph-redesigns last October when they were previewed but I agree with you that they aren't great - and they're certainly not very subtle. Because I think the Ragabash-one does something similar Philodox and Galliard in being way too symbolic (and it's done in a way that suggests a human and not werewolves from a mythical age came up with this).<br /> <br /> The new Ragabash-glyph is actually... the letter Q.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T11:25:32-07:00","id":1511892,"title":"","content":"I think the idea is to keep the old symbol (an empty circle for the new moon), and then some flourish. I'm not sure if they're two daggers (sneaky stabby types) or hands clapping (jokesters) or what... because otherwise it's a Q with a second line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T12:37:43-07:00","id":1511898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511871-auspice-preview-except-ahroun-for-w5?p=1511892#post1511892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the idea is to keep the old symbol (an empty circle for the new moon), and then some flourish. I'm not sure if they're two daggers (sneaky stabby types) or hands clapping (jokesters) or what... because otherwise it's a Q with a second line.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also flattens the meaning of the glyphs. Because running into a rock that is covered in glyphs without knowing what they are should feel eerie. These are a bit too over-designed and too obvious in a way that hurts the point of the Old vs New conflict. The glyphs should feel ancient, not a scale or a lyre OR a Q.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T05:16:07-07:00","id":1512000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511871-auspice-preview-except-ahroun-for-w5?p=1511892#post1511892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the idea is to keep the old symbol (an empty circle for the new moon), and then some flourish. I'm not sure if they're two daggers (sneaky stabby types) or hands clapping (jokesters) or what... because otherwise it's a Q with a second line.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm half-joking with the Q-thing of course but well... it does look like a Q.<br /> <br /> Not only are these glyphs looking worse (they seem &quot;overdesigned&quot; now) but I'm also not sure why it was necessary to do this. I get it, &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot; but then wouldn't it be more logical to <i>either </i>keep the old ones <i>or </i>design new ones...? Who thought it was a good idea to take the old ones and add stuff to them...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T23:06:25-07:00","id":1512087,"title":"","content":"The arts a bit bland (again) but nice clear write up","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T23:45:11-07:00","id":1512089,"title":"","content":"While it might be clearer with the full text, there's a lot that's unclear because the full context of the new setting has been so sparse in the previews.<br /> <br /> For example, the Ragabash get the most &quot;latitude&quot; because of their role as tricksters and questioners... but why? That status was protected by the Litany that most young Garou don't care about any more. The Ragabash being allowed to poke holes in their own allies' plans and egos is part of the &quot;old ways that got us the Apocalypse.&quot; It's not just a need to explain how things are different from older take on things, but the previews have thus far indicated that the failure of the old traditions is a relatively recent event, but the Tribe and Auspice previews thus far haven't really touch on the &quot;now vs. then&quot; aspect of a pivotal aspect of the W5 take on the setting.<br /> <br /> The art isn't just bland, it's crowding out a really important thing to clarify: How do Ragabash due their duties without the cultural institution of the Garou Nation protecting them from reprisals? What are the Theurges and Philodoxes basing their activities on with broken lines of oral traditions caused by the fracturing of bonds that used to hold the Garou together as a larger society? What does building up hype or recording detailed lore really mean for the Galliards of this new normal?<br /> <br /> The previews have said that a large part of the drama of the new setting is that the Garou are trying to figure out what to do with a major upheaval among their kind... and it's entirely unclear how Auspices play into that, and what challenges face them as their roles will adapt as the generations that lived the old ways die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T00:40:26-07:00","id":1512093,"title":"","content":"The whole portrayal of Apocalypse has been... &quot;wishy-washy&quot; thus far, I would say. You start with a bang on pg 10 in the Introduction:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This generation of Garou dwells in the midst of Apocalypse. It\u2019s too late to avert the end.\u200b </div> </div> </div>&quot;It's too late&quot; is quite the sentiment when it comes to an Apocalypse, of course. But just a page further and things are already getting a bit confused:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Apocalypse has happened or is happening, and now it\u2019s up to each pack of Garou to strike back in a way that its members find meaningful.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Well, clearly the Apocalypse has not happened because the world is still there. And this isn't another version of an idea like &quot;cyclical Gehenna&quot; because in the glossary &quot;Apocalypse&quot; is defined like this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Apocalypse: The physical and spiritual end of the world, brought about by relentless human greed and consumption\u200b </div> </div> </div>And yet sometimes you get these moments like with the Ragabash-bit where the Apocalypse is mentioned but then in the Tribe-write-ups it somehow never comes up with the Hart Wardens and is only offhandedly mentioned in the Glass Walkers section. Or on pg 44 and 45 where the text talks about &quot;war against the Apocalypse&quot; which seems a bit weird. Shouldn't it be &quot;the war against the Wyrm&quot;, if anything? And if it's the Apocalypse... so is it too late to avert it or not?<br /> <br /> The ideas of &quot;mid-Apocalypse&quot; and &quot;the Garou-Nation has fallen&quot; should have a <i>huge </i>impact on the setting but so far in the previews it doesn't feel like it's the big deal it should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T01:27:26-07:00","id":1512100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511871-auspice-preview-except-ahroun-for-w5?p=1512093#post1512093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The ideas of &quot;mid-Apocalypse&quot; and &quot;the Garou-Nation has fallen&quot; should have a <i>huge </i>impact on the setting but so far in the previews it doesn't feel like it's the big deal it should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you know what it feels like? It feels like once the Nation fell, the younger garou breathed a sigh of relief and just returned to their normal lives with nary a look behind. Once there were no elders to boss them around, they frankly couldn't care less about the Apocalypse or Gaia. They just want to do their jobs or do their hobbies, the Rage being an annoyance more than the primal anger at the destruction of the world.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T09:52:32-07:00","id":1512122,"title":"","content":"Worse than that, it's pretty realistic if you think about it, unless you think it's personal or you've been raised in the Garou nation for as long as you can remember, it's weird for you to give up your personal life to join a war you don't know. is known, even more so if you think you can use your skills for personal gain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T09:55:44-07:00","id":1512124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511871-auspice-preview-except-ahroun-for-w5?p=1511892#post1511892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the idea is to keep the old symbol (an empty circle for the new moon), and then some flourish. I'm not sure if they're two daggers (sneaky stabby types) or hands clapping (jokesters) or what... because otherwise it's a Q with a second line.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's two crossed claws kind of like a symbol of silence, kind of referring to the garou portrayed in the image.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T10:21:40-07:00","id":1512126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511871-auspice-preview-except-ahroun-for-w5?p=1512122#post1512122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worse than that, it's pretty realistic if you think about it, unless you think it's personal or you've been raised in the Garou nation for as long as you can remember, it's weird for you to give up your personal life to join a war you don't know. is known, even more so if you think you can use your skills for personal gain.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference between W5 and older editions is that no matter what a garou tried they could not slot back into human society. The Curse kept people away and Rage was always bubbling, but there were other reasons blending in was hard. For one, the feeling of spiritual decay and wrongness in cities and suburbs was often hard to take. Unless you were a Gnawer or a GW, living in cities was stifling like being in a too-hot sauna. Even GWs and Gnawers had trouble dealing with it.<br /> <br /> Unless you were a trust fund baby, a ronin would find it easier just living on the run.<br /> <br /> That is one reason the werewolf seems lost in W5's texts, there is no sense of unease among civilization. There is no feeling of being a caged animal or an urban predator. It's just like the character undid their First Change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T12:57:45-07:00","id":1512135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511871-auspice-preview-except-ahroun-for-w5?p=1512124#post1512124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's two crossed claws kind of like a symbol of silence, kind of referring to the garou portrayed in the image.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing in the older books that would back up this interpretation, and if they're tossing out the old glyph language anyway, than anything else we come up with is speculation since any symbol can mean anything until W5 actually starts defining stuff.<br /> <br /> How does two crossed claws relate to someone holding one finger perpendicular to their lips to signify silence? How is anyone supposed to look at the Ragabash glyph and make that connection?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T16:33:00-07:00","id":1512158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511871-auspice-preview-except-ahroun-for-w5?p=1511891#post1511891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The new Ragabash-glyph is actually... the letter Q.</div> </div> </div> </div>My friend said, &quot;Look, it's Q-Anon, emerging from his mother's basement.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T17:04:00-07:00","id":1512161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511871-auspice-preview-except-ahroun-for-w5?p=1512135#post1512135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's nothing in the older books that would back up this interpretation, and if they're tossing out the old glyph language anyway, than anything else we come up with is speculation since any symbol can mean anything until W5 actually starts defining stuff.<br /> <br /> How does two crossed claws relate to someone holding one finger perpendicular to their lips to signify silence? How is anyone supposed to look at the Ragabash glyph and make that connection?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he just thought it was cool, I've seen this comparison done before and maybe the intention is to do a soft rebot, with so much things that have changed I wouldn't be surprised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T17:13:11-07:00","id":1512163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511871-auspice-preview-except-ahroun-for-w5?p=1512126#post1512126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The difference between W5 and older editions is that no matter what a garou tried they could not slot back into human society. The Curse kept people away and Rage was always bubbling, but there were other reasons blending in was hard. For one, the feeling of spiritual decay and wrongness in cities and suburbs was often hard to take. Unless you were a Gnawer or a GW, living in cities was stifling like being in a too-hot sauna. Even GWs and Gnawers had trouble dealing with it.<br /> <br /> Unless you were a trust fund baby, a ronin would find it easier just living on the run.<br /> <br /> That is one reason the werewolf seems lost in W5's texts, there is no sense of unease among civilization. There is no feeling of being a caged animal or an urban predator. It's just like the character undid their First Change.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could be it, it's just my guess, but maybe with Gaia weakened she can no longer keep that feeling in the Garou, this could be a way for her to exert control, but now that the fight is &quot;over&quot; now it's every man for himself so no there's nothing more to control. Or they will just give a Retcon anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T18:38:13-07:00","id":1512171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511871-auspice-preview-except-ahroun-for-w5?p=1512163#post1512163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That could be it, it's just my guess, but maybe with Gaia weakened she can no longer keep that feeling in the Garou, this could be a way for her to exert control, but now that the fight is &quot;over&quot; now it's every man for himself so no there's nothing more to control. Or they will just give a Retcon anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gaia's weakening in prior editions would have likely been felt as a very, very deep pain. This is based off of the Garou and other moon-based Fera getting angina-like pains if/when Luna took an asteroid hit in the Ragnarok scenario of Apocalypse. Think more like Attunement from Trinity, or Obi Wan's reaction to Alderaan being blown up in A New Hope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T18:54:08-07:00","id":1512176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511871-auspice-preview-except-ahroun-for-w5?p=1512171#post1512171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gaia's weakening in prior editions would have likely been felt as a very, very deep pain. This is based off of the Garou and other moon-based Fera getting angina-like pains if/when Luna took an asteroid hit in the Ragnarok scenario of Apocalypse. Think more like Attunement from Trinity, or Obi Wan's reaction to Alderaan being blown up in A New Hope.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or maybe is also one form of control, she is making then feel her pain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T19:05:34-07:00","id":1512178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511871-auspice-preview-except-ahroun-for-w5?p=1512176#post1512176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or maybe is also one form of control, she is making then feel her pain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf is ill-served by this variety of angst wallowing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T19:23:56-07:00","id":1512180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511871-auspice-preview-except-ahroun-for-w5?p=1512178#post1512178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolf is ill-served by this variety of angst wallowing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll try to remember that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T00:50:21-07:00","id":1512191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511871-auspice-preview-except-ahroun-for-w5?p=1512171#post1512171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gaia's weakening in prior editions would have likely been felt as a very, very deep pain. This is based off of the Garou and other moon-based Fera getting angina-like pains if/when Luna took an asteroid hit in the Ragnarok scenario of Apocalypse. Think more like Attunement from Trinity, or Obi Wan's reaction to Alderaan being blown up in A New Hope.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is actually a thing in W5. It's in the glossary and called &quot;Gaia's Howl&quot;. So pretty much every Garou should be aware of how dire the situation is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T01:15:00-07:00","id":1512192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511871-auspice-preview-except-ahroun-for-w5?p=1512163#post1512163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That could be it, it's just my guess, but maybe with Gaia weakened she can no longer keep that feeling in the Garou, this could be a way for her to exert control, but now that the fight is &quot;over&quot; now it's every man for himself so no there's nothing more to control. Or they will just give a Retcon anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say Gaia weakening would be making controlling your Rage WORSE. Remember that garou are born, not made. The character has never been a normal human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T01:52:51-07:00","id":1512195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511871-auspice-preview-except-ahroun-for-w5?p=1512192#post1512192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say Gaia weakening would be making controlling your Rage WORSE. Remember that garou are born, not made. The character has never been a normal human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why the idea of the Get just losing it and going on a rampage is so easy to understand. As for the rest, the focus seems to be instead on old vs young. But how does that make a difference in the face of the Apocalypse?<br /> <br /> Then again the conflict between Hunters with Drive and hunter-orgs in H5 didn't do a whole lot to improve humanity's lot in the face of supernatural monsters either... I guess these games just really want to have some sort of bad status quo vs good rebellion concept in them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T08:41:26-07:00","id":1512215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511871-auspice-preview-except-ahroun-for-w5?p=1512192#post1512192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say Gaia weakening would be making controlling your Rage WORSE. Remember that garou are born, not made. The character has never been a normal human.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but not all descendants of Garou are Garou, most are Kinfolk you can relate it to genetics, but there's no way to say that Gaia didn't choose one or the other for one reason or another. You might wonder, because if she can choose then why not make all the Kinfolk Garou? the reason would be because if that were the case they would devour everything on the planet eventually, the war of rage is proof of that. That could change in the apocalypse, but as I mentioned, weaker. That said, the Rage would only be presumed to be born with the Garou, but it could be a weapon given by Gaia as well as a collar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T09:00:07-07:00","id":1512216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511871-auspice-preview-except-ahroun-for-w5?p=1512215#post1512215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but not all descendants of Garou are Garou, most are Kinfolk you can relate it to genetics, but there's no way to say that Gaia didn't choose one or the other for one reason or another. You might wonder, because if she can choose then why not make all the Kinfolk Garou? the reason would be because if that were the case they would devour everything on the planet eventually, the war of rage is proof of that. That could change in the apocalypse, but as I mentioned, weaker. That said, the Rage would only be presumed to be born with the Garou, but it could be a weapon given by Gaia as well as a collar.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I meant is that a garou is something you can never not be. They can naturally understand wolves, they can enter the umbra and such. There is no weakening that, because it is inherent to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}